Author: anthnel <141725544+anthnel@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Mon Nov 9 14:04:33 2026 +0100

    feat: put the OCI images table on the activity column and drop the failure copy (DEVDESK-146) (#336)

    The OCI images table now shows each row's state in the activity column
    (a glyph and colour from internal/ui/indicator), as the other migrated
    views do, instead of a textual status. Failed scans are read from the
    memoizer (failedScans) so the table and the footer agree on what failed.

    Column widths grow by 4 cells to fit the indicator and the failure dot.
    The registry browser is out of scope here and is deferred to A-09a2
    (DEVDESK-218).

    Refs: DEVDESK-146
    Entire-Checkpoint: 6ba636f88017

    Co-authored-by: anthnel <anthoni.devops@proton.me>

